  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    Offered: Spring, alternating years.  \n\nPrerequisite: A grade of C or better in CHEM 3324.\n\nContinuation of CHEM 3324.  Early and modern quantum theory, wave mechanics and the Schr&ouml;dinger wave equation, valence bond theory, molecular orbital (MO) theory, computational chemistry, group theory and molecular symmetry, vibrational and rotational spectroscopy. \n\nLecture 3 hours, laboratory 3 hours.\n\n    \n</section>",
